# Credentials. Never committed, in any environment.
#
# These files hold real passwords for QA accounts. The QA directory itself IS tracked
# (that is the point - plans, bug records and test IDs have to survive a clone), so
# these rules are the only thing standing between a password and the remote.
fixtures/*.json

# Per-run artifacts. Regenerated on every run, and the reports are large.
results/*
!results/.gitkeep
runs/*
!runs/.gitkeep
reports/*
!reports/.gitkeep

# Screenshots and captured evidence.
#
# Ignored everywhere except qa/evidence/. Evidence attached to a bug record has to travel with
# it: a GitHub issue cannot hold a local file, so the image is committed and linked. Run-by-run
# screenshots stay out, because they are regenerated every run and would grow the repo forever.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.webp

!evidence/**/*.png
!evidence/**/*.jpg
!evidence/**/*.jpeg
!evidence/**/*.webp
